<Base title="belove · about" description="belove is made by BeingWell Technologies, a public benefit corporation building technology aligned with human wellbeing.">
    <main class="page">
        <a class="wordmark" href="/"><span class="be">be</span><span class="love">love</span></a>
        <h1>about</h1>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>belove is made by BeingWell Technologies, a public benefit corporation. That's a legal structure with a promise inside it: we are accountable not only for making a business work, but for a stated public purpose.</p>
            <blockquote>to develop technology that responds to the uniqueness of every human to support our being well together as a healthy whole.</blockquote>

            <h2>why we exist</h2>
            <p>Most of the technology in your life is optimized for engagement: for clicks, for time on screen, for keeping you there. What you click on is often not what's good for you, and what keeps you scrolling is often the thing you regret afterward.</p>
            <p>We're building the alternative, a home for your digital life that optimizes for your wellbeing alone. We want technology that feels less like a feed and more like something on your side.</p>

            <h2>how we sustain ourselves</h2>
            <p>We don't sell advertising, and we don't monetize your attention. belove will be sustained by people who choose to pay for it. We want a business where we make more money only when you are better served, so that our incentives point in the same direction as yours.</p>

            <h2>what we believe</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Alignment</strong> — technology should be attuned to the wellbeing of the people it touches, not extracting from them.</li>
                <li><strong>Stewardship</strong> — humans should govern technology, with a duty of care for the world it acts on.</li>
                <li><strong>Abundance</strong> — the deepest opportunities are in resonant connection, and success should flow back to everyone it touches.</li>
                <li><strong>Love</strong> — the whole is greater than the sum of its parts when the parts support each other; difference is a strength to be woven together.</li>
                <li><strong>Holism</strong> — we intend to keep growing, as people and as an organization, toward what's best for all of us together.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>say hello</h2>
            <p>We'd love to hear from you: <a href="mailto:hello@being.love">hello@being.love</a></p>
        </div>
    </main>
</Base>
